ackground:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eFed \u0026amp; Policy Watch\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:12px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#60a5fa;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:6px;\"\u003eToday\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eCensus Quarterly Services at 10:00 AM ET, Treasury 17-week Bill closings from 11:00 to 11:30 AM, the 9-year note at noon and 1:00 PM, Commercial Paper at 1:00 PM, and H.15 at 4:15 PM create a concentrated rates and liquidity session.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#fbbf24;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:6px;\"\u003eForward Risk\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eThursday adds EIA gas, WPSR, Treasury bills, the 30-year bond, and H.4.1. The Fed calendar shows the next FOMC meeting on September 15-16 and a 2:30 PM press conference on September 16.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eOmissions and Watch\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOmitted today:\u003c/strong\u003e BLS calendar access returned HTTP 403, so CPI, PPI, employment, and other BLS events were not inferred. BEA shows no release for 2026-09-09; EIA has no same-day inventory release; NAR was not required for today\u0027s verified calendar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWatch:\u003c/strong\u003e The official Fed calendar lists the FOMC meeting as a two-day September 15-16 event, but only the September 16 2:30 PM press conference has a standalone time in the calendar; no separate meeting-statement row was inferred.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eTrading Strategy Note - ES Futures\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;border-left:3px solid #34d399;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#34d399;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\"\u003eBase Case\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eES is 7684.25 overnight against a 765.96 SPY close. The 10:00 AM services release and 11:00 AM to 1:00 PM Treasury sequence are the main decision windows. NFCI remains loose, SOFR is stable, and MOVE is below 80, but 10Y at 4.78% and WTI near 94.07 favor smaller size and no chasing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;border-left:3px solid #f87171;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#f87171;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\"\u003eInvalidation\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eLose 7650 and hold below it, or see 10Y above 4.85% and MOVE back above 80, and the constructive bias is invalidated. A weak Treasury reopening, a sharp oil continuation, or a hawkish rates reaction at H.15 also invalidates continuation assumptions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e"}